    "notes": [
      "Not compared with Leshchinsky & Han's finite-difference strength reduction: on refined meshes cSlope's finite element analysis finds a local failure of the 0.3 m facing blocks into the foundation (V065: 0.86, 0.77 and about 0.27 on three meshes; V066b and V066c give the same factor, so the reinforcement does not take part), which their grid does not resolve; the comparison tests the facing model, not the reinforcement.",
      "commercial program A reports 0.971 (Spencer) and 0.976 (Bishop) with the same Ta = 11.4 kN/m (Table 89.2); cSlope and program D are 4 % higher on the reference circle. The difference is not explained (the reinforcement model of the tiers is the likely cause), so the commercial program A value is not used as a check. L&H 0.98 (finite difference).",
      "cSlope fija options.tolerance = 0.001 (tolerancia del solver) en sus checks; no se importa: ogs usa analysis.tolerance = 1e-05."
    ]
